      "side": 1,
      "message": "[warning] Line 261: 🟡 The patch detects vcpkg with `CMAKE_TOOLCHAIN_FILE MATCHES \"vcpkg\\\\.cmake$\"` at the top, but later behavior gates on `VCPKG_TOOLCHAIN`. If `VCPKG_TOOLCHAIN` is absent in some setups (older/chainloaded toolchains), this can incorrectly run `winmake.py` and re-enable non-vcpkg paths. Define a single local boolean from the initial detection and reuse it consistently.",
      "revId": "56587db7e4ccd710bf41f6dab66e0687a1bb6194",
      "serverId": "1e26b4c1-6b8c-47ff-9df7-501b633d3b5a"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4bedfa41_3d5726a1",
        "filename": "CMakeLists.txt",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 261,
      "author": {
        "id": 90
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-06T19:36:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Intentional. VCPKG_TOOLCHAIN is set by vcpkg.cmake during project(), so it can\u0027t be used before project(); the early regex only sets manifest/triplet defaults. After project(), VCPKG_TOOLCHAIN is the authoritative signal. Reusing the regex result would be wrong for a wrapper toolchain that includes vcpkg.cmake: vcpkg would be active but winmake.py would still run.",
      "parentUuid": "fde091a1_547081bb",
      "revId": "56587db7e4ccd710bf41f6dab66e0687a1bb6194",
      "serverId": "1e26b4c1-6b8c-47ff-9df7-501b633d3b5a"
